tion {:value "350002"} "Giant Slalom, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "350005"} "Slalom, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "350008"} "Combined, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "350011"} "Downhill, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "350013"} "Giant Slalom, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "350016"} "Slalom, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "350019"} "Combined, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "1370"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "1396"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "1422"} "1994"] "\n" [:option {:value "1448"} "1998"] "\n" [:option {:value "1475"} "2002"] "\n" [:option {:value "1503"} "2006"] "\n" [:option {:value "924554"} "2010"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000112"} "2018"] "\n" [:option {:value "19019512"} "2022"] "\n" [:option {:value "15000012"} "2026"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/35"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Super G, Women" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "15 February 2014 — 11:00"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/890"} "Gornolyzhniy Tsenter Rosa Khutor, Mountain Cluster, Krasnaya Polyana"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/350012"} "49 from 24 countries"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Course Setter"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5002095"} "Florian Winkler"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUT"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUT.png"}] "AUT"]]] [:tr {} [:th {:valign "top"} "Details"] [:td {} "Gates: 43" [:br {}] "Length: 2100 m" [:br {}] "Start Altitude: 1580 m" [:br {}] "Vertical Drop: 615 m"]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The women’s Super G was the third Alpine skiing event for females held in Sochi. The race was held as scheduled on Saturday, 15 February, in the " [:a {:href "/venues/890"} "Rosa Khutor Alpine Center"] " and started at an altitude of 1,580 metres between the sections “Devil’s Spine” and “Forest Drop”. During this winter the five World Cup Super Gs were won by " [:a {:href "/athletes/128454"} "Lara Gut"] " (Beaver Creek, Lake Louise, and the second race in Cortina), " [:a {:href "/athletes/110344"} "Tina Weirather"] " (St. Moritz), and " [:a {:href "/athletes/110348"} "Elisabeth Görgl"] " (first race in Cortina) and the current standing saw Gut in the lead ahead of Weirather, " [:a {:href "/athletes/118325"} "Anna Fenninger"] ", and Görgl, the 2011 World Champion. But Weirather was unable to compete after her crash in the last downhill training run when she sustained a shin contusion. " [:a {:href "/athletes/101437"} "Lindsey Vonn"] ", bronze medalist from Vancouver and Super G World Cup winner 2010/11 and 2011/12, also missed the Games after tearing her right ACL twice in 2013, and 2010 gold medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/110752"} "Andrea Fischbacher"] " failed to qualify. This left " [:a {:href "/athletes/101833"} "Tina Maze"] ", the 2010 silver medallist, reigning World Champion from 2013, and winner of the Super G World Cup in 2012/13 as the favorite."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The race started unusually as seven of the first eight starters did not finish the course. When second starter " [:a {:href "/athletes/118406"} "Leanne Smith"] " (USA) came down the course in 1:28.38, she didn’t realise that the next six skiers would fail to finish. Finally " [:a {:href "/athletes/118359"} "Fabienne Suter"] " (SUI) with bib number 9 did complete the course in a respectable 1:26.89, which would eventually place her seventh. Nevertheless her time was not beaten until seven skiers later, when " [:a {:href "/athletes/110675"} "Nicole Hosp"] " (AUT) took the lead in a time of 1:26.18. Her countrywoman, Anna Fenninger then skied the course 0.66 seconds better than Hosp, giving the Austrians the first two places. Tina Maze (SLO) took over the bronze medal place with a time of 1:26.28, but this was short lived as Lara Gut (SUI) went 0.03 seconds faster. In the end the two Austrian leaders were split when Super Combined winner " [:a {:href "/athletes/118418"} "Maria Höfl-Riesch"] " (GER) posted a time of 1:26.07, taking the silver medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Fenninger, who was the third Austrian in a row to win the women’s Super G after " [:a {:href "/athletes/99428"} "Dorfmeister"] " in 2006 and Fischbacher in 2010, won the race with an average speed of 88.40 km/hr, 13.42 metres ahead of Höfl-Riesch. Both Fenninger and Höfl-Riesch used Head skis, while bronze medalist Hosp used Fischer. The gold medal awarded to Fenninger included a fragment of the Chelyabinsk meteor, which burst in a superbolide flash over the Chelyabinsk Oblast and caused a powerful shock wave exactly one year prior to this event, on 15 February 2013."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "18"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/118325"} "Anna Fenninger"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUT"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUT.png"}] "AUT"]] [:td {} "1:25.52"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "22"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/118418"} "Maria Höfl-Riesch"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https: